(obsolete:) Since the beach detective is not Intuitive, nor is he Unintuitive, and he also has an excellent memory and long professional experience of being a private detective, he could be a character who actually solves the mystery in conventional ways and shows up as a foil to explain what's going on from a sane perspective. Since he's been dispatched to solve a mystery surrounding the digsby's, presumably he'll have no idea what the martini killer is because it's only a coincidence that there is a martini killer who kills people in a way themed around martinis on the same day that Reginald killed someone with a martini glass.

Even though so far we've seen a lot of the human side of the beach detective, and having him be the foil who solves the mystery in a conventional way will endear him to us, he actually is like a villain of some sort and will eventually shoot Thomas.

